tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/react-native-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/react-native-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/react-native-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/react-native-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2019-06-21T05:35:07Z","label":{"name":"Resolution: Needs More Information","color":"d4c5f9"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebook/react-native/issues/comments/506909166","html_url":"https://github.com/facebook/react-native/issues/25343#issuecomment-506909166","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebook/react-native/issues/25343","id":506909166,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwNjkwOTE2Ng==","user":{"login":"cabelitos","id":984610,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDYxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/984610?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos","html_url":"https://github.com/cabelitos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cabelitos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-06-29T00:05:08Z","updated_at":"2019-06-29T00:05:08Z","body":"Hello @cani1see, how are you feeling today? I looked at your example and I concluded that this is NOT a react-native bug. You see, at line 23 (https://github.com/cani1see/AnimationDemo/blob/f18418eb545fe5fcb5f631e0c55ca3f7cdfe2970/src/RotateWheel.js#L23) you create a new Animated.Value before starting the animation, which overrides the callback listener register that you did in here https://github.com/cani1see/AnimationDemo/blob/f18418eb545fe5fcb5f631e0c55ca3f7cdfe2970/src/RotateWheel.js#L14\r\n.\r\nYou have two options to fix this problem.\r\nAt line 23 you could replace the\r\n```javascript\r\nthis.rotateDeg = new Animated.Value(0)\r\n```\r\nto\r\n```javascript\r\nthis.rotateDeg.setValue(0)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis would lead to the following implementation\r\n```javascript\r\n  rotateImgDelegate = () => {\r\n    if (!this.state.rotating) {\r\n      this.rotateDeg.setValue(0)\r\n      this.setState({\r\n        rotating: !this.state.rotating,\r\n      }, () => {\r\n        this.rotateImg();\r\n      });\r\n    } else {\r\n      this.rotateToIndex(7)\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr if you really want to create a new Animated.Value you will need to do the following\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n  rotateImgDelegate = () => {\r\n    if (!this.state.rotating) {\r\n      this.rotateDeg = new Animated.Value(0)\r\n       this.rotateDeg.addListener(this.rotateListener)\r\n      this.setState({\r\n        rotating: !this.state.rotating,\r\n      }, () => {\r\n        this.rotateImg();\r\n      });\r\n    } else {\r\n      this.rotateToIndex(7)\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nBy the way, you need to adjust your rotating state toggle since it needs to be updated using the prevState due to react batched state updates. Please look at https://reactjs.org/docs/react-component.html#setstate for more info.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebook/react-native/issues/comments/506909166/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"